// The Austroads combinations (AP-G34-23 Figures 2.7, 2.9 and 2.10), as they were shipped in
// turn-paths.json. Vehicles with trailers are switched off in the add-in for now, so they are kept
// here, where the towing and reversing tests still use them, ready to go back.
//
// A vehicle that tows has "hitch" (its fifth wheel, metres ahead of the centre of its rear axle
// group; negative = behind it) and "trailers", listed front to back. Each trailer has:
//   width
//   front_overhang     body ahead of the coupling: the kingpin's setback from the trailer's front
//   wheelbase          from its coupling (kingpin) back to the centre of its axle group
//   rear_overhang      from the centre of its axle group to its rear
//   hitch              where the next trailer couples on, ahead of this one's axle group (B-double: 0)
//   axles, axle_spacing, track   its axle group, as drawn
// max_articulation_deg: 70 degrees between coupled units (AP-G34-23 3.5).
// Scaled from the figures, which don't dimension them: a prime mover's rear_overhang 1.2 (the back
// of its drive wheels, under the trailer) and an A-trailer's rear_overhang 1.85.
